{
  "$schema": "https://appflare.github.io/catalog/schema/v1.json",
  "slug": "omnimail",
  "name": "OmniMail",
  "summary": "Self-hosted multi-domain webmail on one Worker: mailboxes and users on your own domains through Email Routing, sending through Resend or SendFlare, and external Gmail, Microsoft and other accounts in one place. The interface is in Chinese.",
  "tagline": "Mail for your domains and other inboxes in one place",
  "features": [
    "Create mailboxes for several domains in one browser workspace",
    "Read connected Gmail, Microsoft and other supported inboxes",
    "Send messages and replies with a Resend or SendFlare account",
    "Search messages by sender, subject or body",
    "Invite users and set mailbox storage quotas",
    "Translate messages on request with Workers AI"
  ],
  "alternativeTo": ["Roundcube"],
  "homepage": "https://omnimail.aicnos.com",
  "repo": "mibgb65-cloud/OmniMail",
  "license": "MIT",
  "categories": ["email"],
  // Generated secrets (revision 2), edited help text (revision 3) and field links
  // (revision 4) came after this release was published: revisions, no new build.
  // features and alternatives (revision 5).
  "revision": 5,
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "OmniMail contributors",
      "url": "https://omnimail.aicnos.com",
      "github": "mibgb65-cloud"
    },
    { "name": "mimanchi412", "github": "mimanchi412" }
  ],
  "maintainers": ["MendyLanda"],
  // v1.1.4 is the web and Worker release; the repository's float-v* tags
  // belong to the desktop companion app and are not versions of this entry.
  // The bump bot reads only v-prefixed semver tags, which are the web ones.
  "source": { "ref": "v1.2.0", "sha": "629a8102074a3eb8b66e962b68db7f32e45bc4ce" },
  "install": {
    "packageManager": "npm",
    "wranglerConfig": "wrangler.jsonc",
    "workerName": "omni-mail",
    // The React web app the Worker serves from dist/. Upstream's `build`
    // script runs its lint and type checks first; the bundle is the same.
    "buildCommand": "vite build",
    // Answers without a sign-in, after the API has checked the D1 schema.
    "health": { "path": "/api/config" },
    // Upstream's guide points the zone's catch-all at the Worker. Mail to an
    // address that is not a mailbox in the app is refused during the SMTP
    // exchange and never stored.
    "emailRouting": { "catchAll": true }
  },
  // D1, R2, Queues, Workflows and Workers AI have free tiers, and upstream
  // guards the free D1 daily quota itself (requests past it answer 503 and
  // queued mail waits for the next day). Workers AI only translates messages
  // on request, so it is not a requirement. One cron trigger, every 5 minutes.
  "plan": "free",
  "requires": ["zone", "email-routing", "r2"],
  // Seeded from .dev.vars.example and the README's configuration tables.
  // Not asked for: the per-provider *_CREDENTIALS_KEY secrets are kept for
  // older deployments; new ones use MAIL_CREDENTIALS_KEY alone. Backups need
  // the D1 database id, which exists only after the install; set
  // D1_DATABASE_ID, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID and D1_REST_API_TOKEN in the
  // Worker's settings to turn them on.
  "secrets": [
    {
      // Upstream refuses a token under 32 UTF-8 bytes
      // (email-worker/src/features/auth/setup/setup-security.ts:3,13-16). A
      // generated password is 32 ASCII characters, exactly the minimum, so it
      // only works while the manager generates at least 32. Once setup has
      // run, the first-run endpoint refuses before it reads the token
      // (email-worker/src/features/auth/setup/setup-api.ts:39-41).
      "name": "SETUP_TOKEN",
      "label": "Setup token",
      "help": "You paste it on the first-run page to create the super administrator. After that the first-run page refuses to run again, so the token no longer opens anything. A value of your own needs at least 32 characters.",
      "generate": "password"
    },
    {
      "name": "MAIL_CREDENTIALS_KEY",
      "label": "Mail credentials key",
      "help": "Encrypts the passwords and tokens of connected external mailboxes (Gmail, Microsoft, QQ, NAVER, Yandex, iCloud, Linux DO). Changing it makes saved credentials unreadable.",
      "generate": "password"
    },
    {
      "name": "TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY",
      "label": "Two-factor encryption key",
      "help": "Encrypts administrators' authenticator secrets. Have administrators turn two-factor off before you change it.",
      "generate": "password"
    },
    {
      "name": "RESEND_DOMAIN_CONFIGS",
      "label": "Resend configuration",
      "help": "For sending: JSON with one entry per sender domain, for example {\"example.com\":{\"apiKey\":\"re_...\"}}. Without a sending provider the app still receives mail.",
      "link": { "label": "Get a key", "url": "https://resend.com/api-keys" },
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRETS",
      "label": "Resend webhook signing secrets",
      "help": "A JSON array of the signing secrets of the Resend webhooks pointed at /api/webhooks/resend, to show delivery, bounce and complaint status.",
      "link": { "label": "Add a webhook", "url": "https://resend.com/webhooks" },
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "SENDFLARE_API_KEY",
      "label": "SendFlare API key",
      "help": "Sends through SendFlare instead of Resend, from the address in SendFlare sender below.",
      "link": { "label": "Get a key", "url": "https://sendflare.com/" },
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "SENDFLARE_DOMAIN_CONFIGS",
      "label": "SendFlare configuration",
      "help": "JSON with one entry per sender domain, for example {\"example.com\":{\"apiKey\":\"sf_...\",\"from\":\"mail@example.com\"}}; a matching entry wins over Resend for that domain.",
      "link": { "label": "Get a key", "url": "https://sendflare.com/" },
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY",
      "label": "Turnstile secret key",
      "help": "Set it with the site key below. Needed for public registration with email and password, and for invitations several people can use.",
      "link": {
        "label": "Create a widget",
        "url": "https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/turnstile"
      },
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "LINUX_DO_CLIENT_SECRET",
      "label": "Linux DO Connect client secret",
      "help": "With the client ID below, for signing in with Linux DO.",
      "link": { "label": "Create an OAuth app", "url": "https://connect.linux.do/" },
      "optional": true
    }
  ],
  "vars": [
    {
      "name": "SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL",
      "label": "Super administrator email",
      "help": "The sign-in address of the one super administrator, for example owner@example.com."
    },
    {
      "name": "APP_NAME",
      "label": "Site name",
      "help": "Shown in the app and in authenticator apps.",
      "default": "OmniMail",
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY",
      "label": "Turnstile site key",
      "help": "The public key of the Turnstile widget whose secret key is set above.",
      "link": {
        "label": "Create a widget",
        "url": "https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/turnstile"
      },
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "SENDFLARE_FROM",
      "label": "SendFlare sender",
      "help": "A verified sender address for SendFlare, without a display name.",
      "link": { "label": "Open SendFlare", "url": "https://sendflare.com/" },
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "LINUX_DO_CLIENT_ID",
      "label": "Linux DO Connect client ID",
      "help": "Register the app's address followed by /api/auth/linux-do/callback as the callback URL.",
      "link": { "label": "Create an OAuth app", "url": "https://connect.linux.do/" },
      "optional": true
    },
    {
      "name": "APP_ORIGINS",
      "label": "Extra allowed origins",
      "help": "Comma-separated exact origins of other front ends or browser extensions (chrome-extension://<id>) that may call the API. The app's own address never needs listing.",
      "optional": true
    }
  ],
  "postInstall": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Open {{appUrl}}. The first-run page checks D1, R2, the mail queue, the super administrator email and the setup token; enter a display name, a password and the setup token to create the super administrator. The database is already migrated."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Then add the zone you picked under **系统设置 → 域名管理** (Settings, Domains) and create a mailbox under **管理邮箱地址** (Manage addresses). Its catch-all already reaches the Worker; mail to addresses without a mailbox is refused."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Sending needs a Resend or SendFlare account with a verified sender domain; set its configuration in this app's settings."
    }
  ]
}
